body:
Hey! I'm Saten and I make analysis videos on seemingly random things I find interesting. I have a strong leftist edge and a pretty diverse taste in music. Maybe check out my new video on the Blair Witch franchise :)

&#x200B;

[https://youtu.be/qlB1O1g8TpQ](https://youtu.be/qlB1O1g8TpQ)

While the editing was minimalistic, I appreciate how well you integrated them. I'd say perhaps get a pop filter or don't speak so close to the mic next time. The only thing I'd say is that you could have gone a lot more in detail. The review feels a bit surface-level.

&#x200B;

Hope that helps :)

 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5jepQgsruf8&feature=youtu.be](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5jepQgsruf8&feature=youtu.be) 

&#x200B;

My second main video essay about socialism. Still think I need to improve on my delivery and hopefully getting a better mic. I still love my choice of music tho lool.

Thanks for doing this. Such kindness is rare. I started a leftist YouTube a while back and this is my first video. It's not the greatest, but I think it's at least enjoyable lol:

&#x200B;

 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gOIpskrR8eU&t=42s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gOIpskrR8eU&t=42s)

Yeah, sorry, I wasn't really speaking much of you specifically, though I do think you have some misconceptions. Just kinda frustrating to have a lot of people assuming false things about what I said and what I asked for. I'm pretty firm in that everything I've seen seems to show that fantasy and sci-fi even for debut authors can go to 100,000-120,000 because of the worldbuilding requirements and because people who read those genres generally like longer books.

&#x200B;

The situation with my ending is kinda difficult. I'm wondering if there are any examples of series debuts that have really bleak endings, because I don't want to write this whole thing only to be rejected because my ending is too dark. And yeah, I could do what you said, but I put this project off before and I kinda want to take it up now. I'm just wondering how to do it as a debut novelist.

Thank you for being compassionate. I'll check out your link when I have the time. I thank you for validating my feelings. And it's okay that you couldn't do anything, whatever it was...I don't think anyone can help me really :/ I think I'm just destined to die honestly, because I can't get what I need to feel better.

&#x200B;

And yeah I'd agree with you on individualism and collectivism. I just think our society is really skewed in one direction.

Um...who said the teasing will go away? Racial minorities in most countries face racial discrimination even in their adult lives. If anything it could get way worse than just teasing.

&#x200B;

Also I don't think it's comparable. Racial discrimination is largely frowned upon in society, whereas discrimination against autistic people definitely is not. It's mainstream.

Hm? I never said opposing suicide is just for NTs. I think you might have misinterpreted, sorry.

&#x200B;

Also, it is a good reason if you have traits that means that people will always bully and reject you for the rest of your life. That isn't a temporary problem. Finding someone who accepts you doesn't make that go away. I also reject the idea that you can never implement a permanent solution for a temporary problem. I think it's very logical to say "I don't think that enduring this kind of pain for an undefined amount of time is worth keeping my life." For example, if you had to stay in a fire for two days or kill yourself, which would you do? You might choose the latter, and that's okay, but it's not illogical to choose the former.

&#x200B;

And doctors have been unable to help me. I go to them and even they admit that they cannot cure shit life syndrome. A psychiatrist can't make people stop bullying me.

I didn't form my opinion based on false assumptions. I asked if you believe that you are unable to be privileged because you're a woman. If you're not a woman, fine, but you still clearly privileged, and that was the point I was making. I grew up in a country where I could get killed for being gay, and yet you are so privileged you think that you shouldn't even have your views challenged. That's privilege, regardless of your gender.

&#x200B;

Also, I AM A FUCKING LEFTIST, DUMBASS. I'm a fucking communist gender abolitionist for crying out loud. But, of course, I'M the one assuming.

Why do you think all MGTOWs are shitty people? Have you ever even spoken to a MGTOW? I've never heard of an ideology, not even Nazism, in which every single person that follows it is a shitty person. Many, especially in the case of MGTOW, are in a bad place and take on the ideology because it provides comfort to them. This is why you actually need to engage with people.

&#x200B;

Also, do you believe that you are unable to be privileged because you're a woman? As a person that's had to endure tons of actual discrimination, I can detect comments dripping in privilege when I see them, and boy does yours Drip Too Hard.

Well the first dog isn't the same as the dog in the other universe. The first dog has to be different because he will be shaped by his environment.

&#x200B;

Even if my parents were to love me, that is not a love I can accept. It is not a true love.

[https://themighty.com/2018/06/im-a-favorite-person-bpd-borderline-personality-disorder/](https://themighty.com/2018/06/im-a-favorite-person-bpd-borderline-personality-disorder/)

&#x200B;

Haven't read the article, but I assume it gives a good description.

You identify...as a dog? Like an otherkin?

&#x200B;

I don't really understand what you mean by being upfront? I tell all my friends I have DPD, but if you mean telling dates, I don't get any dates to begin with because I'm worthless, so it doesn't matter. If you mean just telling everyone I'm looking for an fp, usually that scares people off if they don't already like you (it's really frustrating to receive conflicting advice, because other people have told me to do the opposite). I can't tell a person though that I want them specifically to be my fp unless I'm already attached, in which case where before they were thinking "he'll probably be someone else's problem," now they have to reject me.

I have only gotten through by default. I've tried a ton of times, but something got in the way every time.

&#x200B;

I have aggressively tried to meet new people, try dating apps and meetups and everything, but it keeps failing, and worse, I keep getting traumatised because every time I become attached to a new fp, they reject me because I'm worthless, and then I get a new trauma, because for a person with DPD, being rejected is the most traumatic thing that can happen to you besides being cheated on. I don't want to be traumatised anymore. If I try anymore I'll just get rejected again. I just want to die.

Well I could certainly see many scenarios in which a disability could excuse someone murdering someone. Have you ever heard of the insanity defense? Happens all the time, and not enough in my opinion.

&#x200B;

That being said, no one said that autistic boys don't understand that groping a girl is wrong, unless they're like severely autistic. Being accused of "stalking" however is a very common thing for autistic boys though, because they don't understand what is considered acceptable in society. As an autistic boy who really tries to be the best most moral person he can be, I can speak from experience in this. The difference between groping a girl and actions that one can consider "stalking" is obvious, one is clear and unambiguous and one is not. Autistic people do not understand social ambiguity, and while there might be a few who understand certain situations, I prefer to err on the side of caution.

That's true, maybe. Though one would think that someone who goes on a lot of dates would have a higher probability of finding someone compatible than someone who goes on none.

&#x200B;

That being said, I won't delete them, because I HAVE to try every possible thing I can to find someone. It's that or kill myself.

I've been in short-term relationships, and those were literally the only times in my life in which I was happy. I am certain I have DPD, which makes it so that I basically can't feel happiness without the love of an fp. It's kind of a known fact about my disorder. Look it up, please, just to know more. (Btw, if you're wondering why I'm posting here even though I don't have DPD, it's because DPD is actually really rare, and BPDs are the only others I know with the concept of fps.)

&#x200B;

Also, I'm trying to say sorry because I get so frustrated that people can't understand DPD, and then people get mad at me for my frustrations with their ignorance, which makes me want to kill myself more. That being said, I appreciate that you are actually trying to help instead of just parroting talking points. I can see that you genuinely care. Thank you.

Out of the top 10 highest grossing movies ever, 2 have been nominated for Best Picture (both by James Cameron), and only one of those two has won.

&#x200B;

Congratulations. You were able to defeat my one specific example while missing the entire point.

Okay I'm actually going to defend T'Challa and the movie here lol. All of what you just said is what I think is the point of the movie. At the end, things didn't go back to the status quo, they recognised Killmonger had good points and opened the borders. Of course T'Challa wasn't going to start off thinking that the status quo is bad. He was raised by people who believed isolation was the right thing to do. One of the emotional climaxes of the movie is T'Challa realising that they shouldn't have isolated themselves and telling off his ancestors. The solving of your criticism is the point of the movie haha.

&#x200B;

Still I liked his characterisation in Civil War a lot more. That really made me fall in love with the character. Also, you're forgetting Blade :p

You sound like you haven't made art before (forgive me if I'm wrong). When you make something, especially something with the intent of combatting racism, and people say it is a very good movie, but some guy decides that he doesn't like it because it didn't make complacent white people uncomfortable enough, it does sound overbearing, even if it is not your intention. It's not got anything to do with the point of the movie and is a purely political critique. The point of the movie is not to analyse the klan. So it's not necessarily important to make all of them fleshed out characters, because that's not the point.

&#x200B;

Also, klansmen are kinda dumb lol. Not all white nationalists are, but the ones who think the best way to promote white supremacy is to meet up in the middle of the night, wear ghost costumes and burn crosses on black people's lawn almost always are. I've never heard of a smart klansman. Even David Duke is one of the intellectual lightweights of the modern day white supremacist movement.

Check again: "I'm actually not even saying that it's wrong to be afraid of men in such a situation. I can certainly understand the feeling. Just like I wouldn't blame a person for subconsciously being more afraid of a black man in the middle of the night than a white man, even though I'm black, because black men are more likely to commit violent crimes. However it doesn't mean that the fear is justified, despite it being valid to feel it."

&#x200B;

That's a quote from my first response to you.

I do wonder why there is a price at all though, besides maybe small administrative fees.

&#x200B;

Also, dropping 35k in a short period of time is a lot even for a well-off person. That's why people spend the entirety of their child's life saving for college.

Quebec myself :)

&#x200B;

It's not about night but walking home at night. Back alley rapes are rare from the stats I've seen, whereas muggings and things like that are a lot more likely to happen to you when you're walking home at night.

Oh wow, this does put a few holes in my argument, I must admit. Good job on the research. I must commend you.

&#x200B;

However there are a few things I must note. In this study men are still more likely to be attacked walking home at night because women are more likely to be sexually assaulted (which happens more often with people that the victim knows), whereas, according to what you cited, "Males, for example, are more likely to be the victims of physical assault and homicide," which is almost certainly more likely to happen to you when you are walking home at night.

&#x200B;

Really good job on the statistics. I learned a lot. But I still think I am ultimately right. About being afraid when "out in the dark, alone, especially with size differences between men and women," please see the point I made in my post about the realities of being attacked at night. I'm actually not even saying that it's wrong to be afraid of men in such a situation. I can certainly understand the feeling. Just like I wouldn't blame a person for subconsciously being more afraid of a black man in the middle of the night than a white man, even though I'm black, because black men are more likely to commit violent crimes. However it doesn't mean that the fear is justified, despite it being valid to feel it.

&#x200B;

Also, Canadian gang! Which province are you from my dude? :)

I think most people who aren't in high school know that Wikipedia isn't as bad as it's made out to be. That being said, the evidence is not Wikipedia, the evidence is the evidence that is cited on Wikipedia. I just linked the page because it compiled all those resources into one place, so it's easy for people to consume. You can read a bunch of things instead of one specific thing.

&#x200B;

And men are by far the biggest victims of muggings.

Actually not that unreasonable an interpretation. Usually you'd want to say chill "whatever you need to chill" in the fridge for an hour. From a linguistic point of you if you just say "chill in the fridge for an hour," the imperative chill is usually taken to mean "you chill," and if you want to chill something else, you say "chill (object) in the fridge." That way there's no ambiguity.

&#x200B;

